{"step_index":219,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:29:49Z","input_tokens":7850,"cache_read_tokens":383769,"output_tokens":19198,"thinking":"Initial focus is on creating `pipeline/v6_sv_comp.py`, the final script in this sequence, bridging the stage lookdev file with the animation assets. This script's purpose is to assemble the final scene from the separate elements produced by the prior scripts.\n\n\nThe script must flawlessly handle the `@env-2` environment's scene dimensions and specific hooks, especially `scene[\"sv_dimension\"]` driving the visual shifts in `V5_SkyDome` and related lighting. Keyframe adjustments for scene dimension transitions are essential, specifically at frames 788, 790, 1601, and 1603, as these dictate the dimensional transitions within the animation. Ensuring these frame transitions and constants function is critical for visual consistency.\n\n\nThe dimensional transitions require precise keyframe handling at specified frames, crucial for visual fidelity. Potential for `@env-2` exposing helper functions or properties tied to `scene[\"sv_dimension\"]` is now a primary consideration. Blender drivers using `scene[\"sv_dimension\"]` will automatically evaluate across all frames, especially on world, dome, and light properties, simplifying wiring of all exposed custom properties and node group inputs.\n\n\nAll rig FCurves, including those for bone movement, steering, wheel spin, and suspension, require decimation and constant interpolation on even frames, except for the `LINEAR` camera. Material actions like brake heat, rain light, and shift LEDs will step on even frames to ensure a 12 fps aesthetic. However, the camera focus, car lights, and scene exposure will remain linear at 24 fps.\n\n\nFocusing on aerodynamic ribbon animation, the script must implement scaling based on aero conditions and camera positions. Odd frames require constant interpolation for the ribbon scale, based on the `aero_on` value and camera position to achieve the desired flutter effect. The script will use the initial rest scale for each object, derived from an earlier file, applying reduced scale under specific conditions.\n\n\nThe wheel smear effect requires a speed gate t\n<truncated 2996 bytes>\nng offsets to the image painterly effect and combining with the original color generates distinct color channels (Red, Green, Blue) that can be mixed for print misregistration. A mask ensures that the effect is only applied on out-of-focus areas for the \"Spider-Verse\" look.\n\nProceeding to edge detection, utilizing Kirsch and Sobel filters on normal and mist passes is next. The plan involves connecting the normal pass to a Kirsch filter and then to an RGB to BW node, resulting in the `norm_edge` output. Using mist pass to generate `mist_edge`, creating fine graphic edge ink details.\n\n\nKirsch and Sobel filters will produce edge details, using normals for `norm_edge` and mist for `mist_edge`.  These will be combined with fade calculations tied to camera distance and car scale, creating masks to isolate the effect on the background and hero car. Edge details will be blended with a Spider-Verse ink color over the base image for the final inked image.\n\nNext, paper grain and animated radial speed lines will be applied. The paper grain image will be scaled and mixed with the inked image using a soft light blend. Radial speed lines will be added based on vehicle speed exceeding a certain threshold.\n\n\nAnalyzing image processing stages for the graphic impact duotone slam, specifically for frames 312-313 and 1698-1699. Calculating the impact signal (`imp_val`) combines luminosity, emission, speed lines, and car matte to drive two shader ramps for a stark flash and woodcut stencil effect. Shader ramp A uses an inverted color scheme with paper white, electric crimson, and pitch ink black. Shader ramp B uses pitch ink black and electric crimson for the 2099 woodcut stencil.\n\n\nInitial concern focuses on verifying all compositor node connections and data types to prevent errors. A quick test will evaluate four specific frames across different animation acts. The plan involves running the compositor script on an existing file for an immediate error check before the lookdev stage is complete. The goal is 100% zero socket errors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nV6 SPIDER-VERSE ANIMATION RHYTHM (12 FPS ON-TWOS), 3-ACT MULTIVERSE COLOR SCRIPT\\n& MULTI-PASS COMPOSITOR (`Comp_V6_SpiderVerse`)\\n=================================================================================\\n输入: v6_spiderverse/v6_stage_lookdev.blend  (只读输入，绝不修改任何 V5 文件)\\n输出: v6_spiderverse/v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\\n\\n核心特性:\\n  1. 安全抽帧（Safe \\\"On Twos\\\" 12 fps）：\\n     - 世界位移 Bone_Root、航向 Bone_Heading、焦点 V5_CamFocus 与全部 26 机位保持 24 fps LINEAR（零追随抖动）；\\n     - 车体局部次级动态（俯仰/侧倾/方向盘/前轮转向/悬挂/换挡灯/刹车热辉光）及 V6_09_ComicFX 三维速度特效\\n       按 2 帧一拍设为 CONSTANT（正宗 12 fps 手绘动画质感），快门压至 0.07。\\n  2. 三幕平行宇宙色彩剧本 + 次元撕裂转场 + 黑白红高反差冲击帧（Impact Frames）：\\n     - Act I   (f=1..788,    S01..S09) : sv_dimension = 0.0 (Earth-1610 迈尔斯美漫黄昏)\\n     - Portal  (f=788..790)            : 次元故障色散撕裂\\n     - Act II  (f=789..1601, S09b..S18): sv_dimension = 1.0 (Earth-65 格温青紫水彩表现主义)\\n     - Portal  (f=1601..1603)          : 次元故障色散撕裂\\n     - Act III (f=1602..2161, S19..S26): sv_dimension = 2.0 (Earth-928 2099 暗黑紫外霓虹红)\\n     - Impact  (f=312..313 & f=1698..1699): 双帧漫画黑白赤红版画冲击帧（对齐 331 km/h Stowe 重刹与音效重低音）\\n  3. Blender 5.3 多通道合成器 (`Comp_V6_SpiderVerse`)：\\n     - Cryptomatte 精准分离主角赛车（确保主角赛车 100% 锐利，零 Kuwahara 涂抹、零 CMYK 重影模糊）；\\n     - Anisotropic Kuwahara 背景水彩笔触滤镜（Act II 格温宇宙全开）；\\n     - Normal (Kirsch) + Mist (Sobel) 远近自适应屏幕空间墨线（长焦自动减薄防机翼糊黑，远景雾化消隐防闪烁）；\\n     - 焦平面外红青印刷错位（CMYK / Red-Cyan Print Misregistration，替代传统光学虚\n<truncated 34504 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"d:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v6_sv_comp.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
